# NestJS API prefix and response envelope

## Prefix

Every NestJS HTTP app sets the global prefix `v1` in `main.ts`, so routes are `/v1/...`. Never hardcode `v1` in `@Controller()` paths.

```typescript
const app = await NestFactory.create(AppModule, { rawBody: true });
app.setGlobalPrefix('v1');
app.useGlobalInterceptors(new ResponseInterceptor());
app.useGlobalFilters(new AllExceptionsFilter());
```

## Envelope

```typescript
export interface ApiMeta { requestId: string }

export interface ApiSuccess<T> {
  success: true;
  statusCode: number;
  message: string;
  data: T;
  meta: ApiMeta;
}

export interface ApiFailure {
  success: false;
  statusCode: number;
  error: {
    code: string;                  // UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
    message: string;
    details?: { field: string; issue: string }[];
  };
  meta: ApiMeta;
}

export type ApiResponse<T> = ApiSuccess<T> | ApiFailure;
```

Success example (check-in):

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "statusCode": 201,
  "message": "Check-in recorded successfully",
  "data": {
    "attendanceId": "att_9f8e7d6c5b4a",
    "workerId": "wrk_12ab",
    "venueId": "ven_34cd",
    "shiftId": "shf_56ef",
    "matchedAt": "2026-11-03T17:00:00Z",
    "confidence": 0.97
  },
  "meta": { "requestId": "req_abc123xyz789" }
}
```

Fail example (4xx):

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "statusCode": 404,
  "error": {
    "code": "FACE_NOT_MATCHED",
    "message": "No enrolled worker matched the captured face above the confidence threshold.",
    "details": [
      { "field": "confidence", "issue": "Best score 0.42 is below threshold 0.85" }
    ]
  },
  "meta": { "requestId": "req_abc123xyz789" }
}
```

Error (5xx): fixed generic message; log real error + stack with `requestId`; never return stack traces, SQL, or embedding payloads.

## Implementation

- `ResponseInterceptor` wraps handler returns into `ApiSuccess`; use `@ResponseMessage('...')`, default `"OK"`.
- `statusCode` in the body equals the HTTP status.
- `AllExceptionsFilter`: `HttpException` < 500 → `ApiFailure`; `ValidationPipe` → `details`; domain errors via `DomainException(code, message, statusCode, details?)`; else 500 `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR`.
- `meta.requestId`: from `x-request-id` or generate `req_<random>`; echo in response header and logs.
- Document envelopes in Swagger (`@nestjs/swagger`).
- Microservice / queue handlers that return RPC-style results use the same envelope shape via an `RpcExceptionFilter` when applicable.
